# Tech Stack Standards

## Required Stack for Web Apps
Every web app project must explicitly use:
- **Next.js (latest version)**  
- **Tailwind CSS (latest stable)**  
- **Auth.js** for authentication  
- **Resend** for email functionality (if emails are used)  
- **Stripe** for any payment functionality (latest SDK version, secure server-side integration only)  
- **Convex** for all data and file storage needs (as the unified backend layer)  
- **Google Sign-In** as the **initial auth provider** (additional providers can be added later)

## Payment Integration
- When Stripe is used for multi-organization or multi-user payouts, **Stripe Connect** must be implemented for compliant fund distribution.

## Backend Layer
- Convex must handle **database management, file storage, and real-time sync** where applicable.
- Ensure proper configuration for responsive UI, accessibility, and security compliance across all integrations.

## Package Management
- Always use **bun** as the package manager.

## Authentication
- For authentication flows, follow the markdown guides located in `~/Documents/auth0-guide`.
